  "final_message": "Fixed the inconsistency in `grammar/precedence.ebnf`. Since `unary` is level 70 (higher) and `exponent` is level 60 (lower), unary actually binds tighter/before exponent — the example comment previously said the opposite (`exponent-binds-before-unary`), contradicting the stated precedence levels. I corrected it to `unary-binds-before-exponent` while leaving the `unary` and `exponent` production rules untouched.",
